Keith Bradnam (keith@thale.nott.ac.uk) wrote:


: with no further options, this restored my root fileset into the current
: directory, but if I then run 'mt fsf' and repeat 'vrestore -x' it doesn't
: restore my 'home' fileset, but restores the root fileset again.

: What am I doing wrong?  I can't seem to find anything in the vrestore man
: page that explicitly states how to restore whole filesets.

: Hope someone can help,

: Keith

     Assuming your tape drive is mt0 there should have been created
two versions.  Example /dev/rmt0h and /dev/nrmt0h.  The first
autorewinds.  You use the second form with mt -f and it won't rewind
after it fast forwards.

