> After the install, I allocated some extra space (dsk0e) and activated
> it as AdvFS.

What exactly did you do?  The assigning of a partition to AdvFS is
automatically done as part of the mkfdmn command; there is no separate
and prior step required.  Whatever you did beforehand may be tripping up
AdvFS.

Do a "disklabel -r dsk0" and see if the e partition is available and
make sure it's not overlapping an already-in-use partition.  If the
partition passes these two tests you should be able to do a "mkfdmn
/dev/disk/dsk0e shelly_domain."  By the way, make sure the domain didn't
already get created w/o your noticing it; check this by doing a long
recursive listing of /etc/fdmns -- if you see dsk0e in the output then
AdvFS already knows about it that partition and you'll have to use
rmfdmn to get rid of it.

Hth,
WJD


