Daniel Willems wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I'm totally new on True64 ( on any Unix)
> 
> If I want to open a telnet session I get : fork: operation would block
> 
> The logfile shows: task table is full
> 
> What to do ?


Assuming some version of V4.x, the message comes from the kernel fork()
function when you exceed the "task_max" configuration parameter.  Use
the command "sysconfig -q proc" to see the current setting of the
parameter.  The easiest way to fix this is to edit the
"/etc/sysconfigtab" file and add the following 2 lines"

	proc:
	  task_max=xxx

Where xxx is the value you want.  You will need to reboot.

request to all: ALWAYS specify the O/S version number when asking for
advise - thanks!!!

Tony V.
Kernel Group



