Check in you /etc/sysconfigtab, on the bottom, under the 'proc:' heading,
for 'maxusers = xxx'.  If there is nothing like that, enter 'maxusers =
xxx' where xxx is 512, 1024, or 2048.  With no entry, the default is 32.
After you enter that in, reboot the machine, and your machine will allow
more processes.  

If you want to see all the running process, use 'ps aux'.  Then 'kill -9
[pid]'.  

Kevin 

