Our new Compaq XP1000 (running Tru64 5.0a) came with a TZ88 DLT drive.

From the online Compaq support pages I've deduced that after connecting it
all, and then rebooting it detects the tape drive.  Running the 'hwmgr
-view devices' command gives me:

 53: /dev/ntape/tape0     DEC      TZ88     (C) DEC bus-3-targ-5-lun-0

I have managed to access the tape drive using the 'tapex' command, but I
was curious whether this was *all* I had to do to bring this machine
on-line, I haven't found any further instructions that tell me I need to
configure it.  So I guess my questions (based on my zero experience of
configuring SCSI devices) are:

1) Is that it in terms of basic configuration?

2) Do I just use /dev/ntape/tape0 to point to this device?

3) Can anyone recommend decent backup software?  The networker software
that comes with Tru64 is evaluation only.  I have heard of 'amanda' are
there any others out there, or do people suggest I just use 'dump' myself
on some sort of cronjob?

If anybody can point me to a website that would be appreciated, as my own
trawling of the web haven't found too much so far.

Thanks,

Keith


