In article <8jqnut$vde$1@nnrp1.deja.com>, ntavera@my-deja.com writes:

>Can I use a HP Autoloader with a PWS 433au? Also I want to know if I
>can change the tape from a shell script?

If the loader supports a sequential mode like many media changers
and with a suitable DDR entry for the tape drive it should work
fine.  You can use mt(1) with the "offline" command to change
media sequentially if it works that way.

If it also supports random access, the Media Robot Utility may
work, if the changer is well behaved.  The only HP device it
was ever tested with was a 16 slot optical library, but that
was well behaved.

As for the system itself, you'll probably need a supported
add-on SCSI adapter.  As I recollect, the internal cable length
of the built-in adapter, was too close to the Fast-20 SCSI
limit to allow external devices.

