Ok, I don't know if in Tru64 5.0 things are working different, but up to
version 4.0f
I always used:

#fddisk -fmt /dev/fd0a                        to format (man fddisk)

#disklabel -wr /dev/fd0c RX23           to label (man disklabel)

#newfs /dev/fd0c RX23                      to initialize ufs file system
(man newfs)

#mount /dev/fd0c /mountpoint             to mount it (man mount)

You can work with this "cop with" instructions; obviously the disk is to be
used only in Tru64 systems.

