> > We had to move the server into a new networking environment.
> > The switches/hubs on the net require that the server should be 100 Mb full
> > duplex to pass packets trough.
> >
> > Any one any idea?
> >

Is the network interface capable of 100 MB FD ? If not, I think the best
solution
is to buy a new one.

In the console you can try
>>> set ewa0_mode
to see what modes are available (that'll tell you whether you can go to 100 MB
FD)
and you can either set it to auto_negociate or force it to 100MB FD.

Also, some switches allow ports to be configured to e.g. 10MB half duplex.

Hope this helps,

Pedro.




