> It's depend from your graphic card.
> Here a example for the Elsa Gloria Synergy 8MB (4D10T,PBXGI-AD)
>
> To change the visual type, modify the
> "Xserver.conf"  file in  "/var/X11/" or "/usr/var/X11/"
>
> Add the the following switches to the command line
> argument section to change the resoluion to 1024x768,
> 24 bits per pixel,  at 75hz.
>
> args <
>       -pn -screen 1024x768 -depth 24 -vsync 75
> >
>
> Notice that "-depth 24" is used instead of
> "-vclass TrueColor"
>
> The -screen 1024x768 and -vsync 75  are for example
> only.  You should use a resolution and vertical sync
> that are compatible with your monitor.
>
> The Xserver must be restarted to have the new settings
> take affect.
>
> XDM = /sbin/init.d/xdm  stop
>       /sbin/init.d/xdm  start
>
